\s1 Everything Is Futile
\p \v 1 \rb These are the words|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the Teacher|קֹהֶ֣לֶת\rb*,\f + \fr 1:1 \ft Or \fqa the Convener \ft or \fqa the Preacher \ft or \fqa the leader of the assembly\ft ; Hebrew \fqa Qoheleth \ft is rendered as \fqa the Teacher \ft throughout Ecclesiastes.\f* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, \rb king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb Futility|הֲבֵ֤ל\rb*\f + \fr 1:2 \ft Literally \fqa vapor \ft or \fqa breath\ft ; the Hebrew words translated in Ecclesiastes as forms of \fqa futile \ft or \fqa fleeting \ft can also be translated as \fqa vanity \ft or \fqa meaningless\ft .\f* \rb of futilities|הֲבָלִים֙\rb*,”
\q2 \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the Teacher|קֹהֶ֔לֶת\rb*,
\q1 “\rb futility|הֲבֵ֥ל\rb* \rb of futilities|הֲבָלִ֖ים\rb*!
\q2 \rb Everything|הַכֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb is futile|הָֽבֶל׃\rb*!”
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb does a man|לָֽאָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb gain|יִּתְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb from all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb his labor|עֲמָל֔וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb at which he toils|שֶֽׁיַּעֲמֹ֖ל\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 4 \rb Generations|דּ֤וֹר\rb* \rb come|הֹלֵךְ֙\rb* \rb and generations|וְד֣וֹר\rb* \rb go|בָּ֔א\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the earth|וְהָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb remains|עֹמָֽדֶת׃\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֥ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb The sun|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb* \rb rises|וְזָרַ֥ח\rb* \rb and the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb* \rb sets|וּבָ֣א\rb*;
\q2 \rb it hurries back|שׁוֹאֵ֛ף\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֨ל־\rb* \rb to|מְקוֹמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb where|שָֽׁם׃\rb* \rb it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb rises|זוֹרֵ֥חַֽ\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb The wind|הָר֔וּחַ\rb* \rb blows|הוֹלֵךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb southward|דָּר֔וֹם\rb*,
\q2 \rb then turns|וְסוֹבֵ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb northward|צָפ֑וֹן\rb*;
\q1 \rb round|סוֹבֵ֤ב׀\rb* \rb and round|סֹבֵב֙\rb* \rb it swirls|הוֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb ever returning|שָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb its|הָרֽוּחַ׃\rb* \rb course|סְבִיבֹתָ֖יו\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the rivers|הַנְּחָלִים֙\rb* \rb flow|הֹלְכִ֣ים\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb yet the sea|וְהַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb is never|אֵינֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb full|מָלֵ֑א\rb*;
\q1 \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|מְק֗וֹם\rb* \rb from which the streams|שֶׁ֤הַנְּחָלִים֙\rb* \rb come|הֹֽלְכִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb there|שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb again|שָׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb they|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb flow|לָלָֽכֶת׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb things|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb are wearisome|יְגֵעִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb more|לֹא־\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֥ל\rb* \rb than one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb can describe|לְדַבֵּ֑ר\rb*;
\q1 \rb the eye|עַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb satisfied|תִשְׂבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb with seeing|לִרְא֔וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb nor|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb the ear|אֹ֖זֶן\rb* \rb content|תִמָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb with hearing|מִשְּׁמֹֽעַ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb has been|שֶּֽׁהָיָה֙\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb will be again|שֶׁיִּהְיֶ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and what|וּמַה־\rb* \rb has been done|שֶׁנַּֽעֲשָׂ֔ה\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb will be done again|שֶׁיֵּעָשֶׂ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb there is nothing|וְאֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb new|חָדָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Is there a case|יֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb where one can say|שֶׁיֹּאמַ֥ר\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֛ר\rb*,
\q2 “\rb Look|רְאֵה־\rb*, \rb this|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb is new|חָדָ֣שׁ\rb*”?
\q1 \rb It|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb has already|כְּבָר֙\rb* \rb existed|הָיָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb in the ages|לְעֹֽלָמִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb before us|מִלְּפָנֵֽנוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb There is no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb remembrance|זִכְר֖וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb of those who came before|לָרִאשֹׁנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וְגַ֨ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb and those yet to come|לָאַחֲרֹנִ֜ים\rb* \rb will not be|שֶׁיִּהְי֗וּ\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb remembered|זִכָּר֔וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb by|עִ֥ם\rb* \rb those who|שֶׁיִּהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb follow|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb after|לָאַחֲרֹנָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\s1 With Wisdom Comes Sorrow
\p \v 12 \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb*, \rb the Teacher|קֹהֶ֗לֶת\rb*, \rb was|הָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb king|מֶ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb And I set|וְנָתַ֣תִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my mind|לִבִּ֗י\rb* \rb to seek|לִדְר֤וֹשׁ\rb* \rb and explore|וְלָתוּר֙\rb* \rb by wisdom|בַּֽחָכְמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |עַ֛ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is done|נַעֲשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb What|ה֣וּא׀\rb* \rb a miserable|רָ֗ע\rb* \rb task|עִנְיַ֣ן\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb has laid|נָתַ֧ן\rb* \rb upon the sons|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of men|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb to occupy them|לַעֲנ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |בּֽוֹ׃\rb*!
\p \v 14 \rb I have seen|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the things|הַֽמַּעֲשִׂ֔ים\rb* \rb that are done|שֶֽׁנַּעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and have found them|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb all|הַכֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb to be futile|הֶ֖בֶל\rb*, \rb a pursuit|וּרְע֥וּת\rb* \rb of the wind|רֽוּחַ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb What is crooked|מְעֻוָּ֖ת\rb* \rb cannot|לֹא־\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֣ל\rb* \rb be straightened|לִתְקֹ֑ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and what is lacking|וְחֶסְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb cannot|לֹא־\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֥ל\rb* \rb be counted|לְהִמָּנֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb said|דִּבַּ֨רְתִּי\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb myself|לִבִּי֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb I|אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb have grown|הִגְדַּ֤לְתִּי\rb* \rb and increased|וְהוֹסַ֙פְתִּי֙\rb* \rb in wisdom|חָכְמָ֔ה\rb* \rb beyond|עַ֛ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb those|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנַ֖י\rb* \rb who were|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and my mind|וְלִבִּ֛י\rb* \rb has observed|רָאָ֥ה\rb* \rb a wealth|הַרְבֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb of wisdom|חָכְמָ֥ה\rb* \rb and knowledge|וָדָֽעַת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb So I set|וָאֶתְּנָ֤ה\rb* \rb my mind|לִבִּי֙\rb* \rb to know|לָדַ֣עַת\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וְדַ֥עַת\rb* \rb madness|הוֹלֵל֖וֹת\rb* \rb and folly|וְשִׂכְל֑וּת\rb*; \rb I learned|יָדַ֕עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb this|ה֖וּא\rb*, \rb too|שֶׁגַּם־\rb*, \rb is a pursuit|רַעְי֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the wind|רֽוּחַ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb with much|בְּרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb comes much|רָב־\rb* \rb sorrow|כָּ֑עַס\rb*,
\q2 \rb and as knowledge|דַּ֖עַת\rb* \rb grows|וְיוֹסִ֥יף\rb*, \rb grief|מַכְאֽוֹב׃\rb* \rb increases|יוֹסִ֥יף\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 The Futility of Pleasure
\p \v 1 \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֤רְתִּֽי\rb* \rb to myself|בְּלִבִּ֔י\rb*, “\rb Come|לְכָה־\rb* \rb now|נָּ֛א\rb*, \rb I will test|אֲנַסְּכָ֛ה\rb* \rb you with pleasure|בְשִׂמְחָ֖ה\rb*; \rb enjoy|וּרְאֵ֣ה\rb* \rb what is good|בְט֑וֹב\rb*!”
\p \rb But it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb proved|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb* \rb to be futile|הָֽבֶל׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb I said|אָמַ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb of laughter|לִשְׂח֖וֹק\rb*, “\rb It is folly|מְהוֹלָ֑ל\rb*,” \rb and of pleasure|וּלְשִׂמְחָ֖ה\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb does it|זֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb accomplish|עֹשָֽׂה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 3 \rb I sought|תַּ֣רְתִּי\rb*\rb |בְלִבִּ֔י\rb* \rb to cheer my body|בְּשָׂרִ֑י\rb*\rb |לִמְשׁ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb with wine|בַּיַּ֖יִן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and to embrace|וְלֶאֱחֹ֣ז\rb* \rb folly|בְּסִכְל֔וּת\rb*— \rb my mind|וְלִבִּ֞י\rb* \rb still guiding me|נֹהֵ֤ג\rb* \rb with wisdom|בַּֽחָכְמָה֙\rb*— \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I could see|אֶרְאֶ֗ה\rb* \rb what|אֵי־\rb* \rb was|זֶ֨ה\rb* \rb worthwhile|ט֜וֹב\rb* \rb for men|לִבְנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |הָאָדָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb to do|יַעֲשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb during the few|מִסְפַּ֖ר\rb* \rb days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their lives|חַיֵּיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb I expanded|הִגְדַּ֖לְתִּי\rb* \rb my pursuits|מַעֲשָׂ֑י\rb*. \rb I built|בָּנִ֤יתִי\rb*\rb |לִי֙\rb* \rb houses|בָּתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and planted|נָטַ֥עְתִּי\rb* \rb vineyards|כְּרָמִֽים׃\rb* \rb for myself|לִ֖י\rb*. \v 5 \rb I made|עָשִׂ֣יתִי\rb* \rb gardens|גַּנּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and parks|וּפַרְדֵּסִ֑ים\rb* \rb for myself|לִ֔י\rb*, \rb where|בָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb I planted|וְנָטַ֥עְתִּי\rb* \rb all kinds|כָּל־\rb* \rb of fruit|פֶּֽרִי׃\rb* \rb trees|עֵ֥ץ\rb*. \v 6 \rb I built|עָשִׂ֥יתִי\rb*\rb |לִ֖י\rb* \rb reservoirs|בְּרֵכ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |מָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to water|לְהַשְׁק֣וֹת\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb my groves|יַ֖עַר\rb* \rb of flourishing|צוֹמֵ֥חַ\rb* \rb trees|עֵצִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb I acquired|קָנִ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb menservants|עֲבָדִ֣ים\rb* \rb and maidservants|וּשְׁפָח֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and servants were born|וּבְנֵי־\rb* \rb in my house|בַ֖יִת\rb*. \rb I also|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb owned|הָ֣יָה\rb* \rb more|הַרְבֵּה֙\rb* \rb herds|בָקָ֨ר\rb*\rb |מִקְנֶה֩\rb* \rb and flocks|וָצֹ֤אן\rb* \rb than anyone|מִכֹּ֛ל\rb*\rb |שֶֽׁהָי֥וּ\rb*\rb |הָ֣יָה\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנַ֖י\rb*, \v 8 \rb and I|גַּם־\rb* \rb accumulated|כָּנַ֤סְתִּי\rb* \rb for myself|לִי֙\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb and the treasure|וּסְגֻלַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of kings|מְלָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb and provinces|וְהַמְּדִינ֑וֹת\rb*. \rb I gathered|עָשִׂ֨יתִי\rb* \rb to myself|לִ֜י\rb* \rb male and|שָׁרִ֣ים\rb* \rb female singers|וְשָׁר֗וֹת\rb*, \rb and the delights|וְתַעֲנוּגֹ֛ת\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of men|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* — \rb many|שִׁדָּ֥ה\rb* \rb concubines|וְשִׁדּֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb So I became great|וְגָדַ֣לְתִּי\rb* \rb and surpassed|וְהוֹסַ֔פְתִּי\rb* \rb all|מִכֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb who had preceded me|שֶׁהָיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |לְפָנַ֖י\rb*; \rb and|אַ֥ף\rb* \rb my wisdom|חָכְמָתִ֖י\rb* \rb remained|עָ֥מְדָה\rb* \rb with me|לִּֽי׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Anything|וְכֹל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb my eyes|עֵינַ֔י\rb* \rb desired|שָֽׁאֲל֣וּ\rb*, \rb I did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb deny myself|אָצַ֖לְתִּי\rb*.\rb |מֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb I refused|מָנַ֨עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my heart|לִבִּ֜י\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |מִכָּל־\rb* \rb pleasure|שִׂמְחָ֗ה\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb my heart|לִבִּ֤י\rb* \rb took delight|שָׂמֵ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb in all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb my work|עֲמָלִ֔י\rb*, \rb and this|וְזֶֽה־\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the reward|חֶלְקִ֖י\rb* \rb for all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb my labor|עֲמָלִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Yet when I|אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb considered|וּפָנִ֣יתִֽי\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the works|מַעֲשַׂי֙\rb* \rb that my hands|יָדַ֔י\rb* \rb had accomplished|שֶֽׁעָשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb and what|וּבֶֽעָמָ֖ל\rb* \rb I had toiled|שֶׁעָמַ֣לְתִּי\rb* \rb to achieve|לַעֲשׂ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb I found|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb everything|הַכֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb to be futile|הֶ֙בֶל֙\rb*, \rb a pursuit|וּרְע֣וּת\rb* \rb of the wind|ר֔וּחַ\rb*; \rb there was nothing|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb to be gained|יִתְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\s1 The Wise and the Foolish
\p \v 12 \rb Then I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb turned|וּפָנִ֤יתִֽי\rb* \rb to consider|לִרְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and madness|וְהוֹלֵל֖וֹת\rb* \rb and folly|וְסִכְל֑וּת\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb what more|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb can the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הָאָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb successor|שֶׁיָּבוֹא֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb do|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb than what has already|כְּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb been accomplished|עָשֽׂוּהוּ׃\rb*? \v 13 \rb And I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb saw|וְרָאִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb that|שֶׁיֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb wisdom|לַֽחָכְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb exceeds|יִתְר֛וֹן\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb folly|הַסִּכְל֑וּת\rb*, \rb just as light|הָא֖וֹר\rb* \rb exceeds|כִּֽיתְר֥וֹן\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb darkness|הַחֹֽשֶׁךְ׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb The wise|הֶֽחָכָם֙\rb* \rb man has eyes|עֵינָ֣יו\rb* \rb in his head|בְּרֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the fool|וְהַכְּסִ֖יל\rb* \rb walks|הוֹלֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb in darkness|בַּחֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb*.
\p \rb Yet I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb also|גַם־\rb* \rb came to realize|וְיָדַ֣עְתִּי\rb* \rb that one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb fate|שֶׁמִּקְרֶ֥ה\rb* \rb overcomes|יִקְרֶ֥ה\rb* \rb them|אֶת־\rb* \rb both|כֻּלָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb So I|אֲנִ֜י\rb* \rb said|וְאָמַ֨רְתִּֽי\rb* \rb to myself|בְּלִבִּ֗י\rb*, “\rb The fate|כְּמִקְרֵ֤ה\rb* \rb of the fool|הַכְּסִיל֙\rb* \rb will also|גַּם־\rb* \rb befall|יִקְרֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb me|אֲנִ֣י\rb*. \rb What|וְלָ֧מָּה\rb* \rb then|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb have I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb gained|יוֹתֵ֑ר\rb* \rb by being wise|חָכַ֛מְתִּי\rb*?”
\p \rb And I said|וְדִבַּ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb to myself|בְלִבִּ֔י\rb* \rb that this|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb too|שֶׁגַּם־\rb* \rb is futile|הָֽבֶל׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֨ין\rb* \rb lasting|לְעוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb remembrance|זִכְר֧וֹן\rb* \rb of the wise|לֶחָכָ֛ם\rb*, \rb just as with|עִֽם־\rb* \rb the fool|הַכְּסִ֖יל\rb*, \rb seeing that|בְּשֶׁכְּבָ֞ר\rb* \rb both|הַכֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb will be forgotten|נִשְׁכָּ֔ח\rb* \rb in the days|הַיָּמִ֤ים\rb* \rb to come|הַבָּאִים֙\rb*. \rb Alas|וְאֵ֛יךְ\rb*, \rb the wise man|הֶחָכָ֖ם\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֥וּת\rb* \rb just like|עִֽם־\rb* \rb the fool|הַכְּסִֽיל׃\rb*! \v 17 \rb So I hated|וְשָׂנֵ֙אתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb life|הַ֣חַיִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the work|הַֽמַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb that is done|שֶׁנַּעֲשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb* \rb was grievous|רַ֤ע\rb* \rb to me|עָלַי֙\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb everything|הַכֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb is futile|הֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb and a pursuit|וּרְע֥וּת\rb* \rb of the wind|רֽוּחַ׃\rb*.
\s1 The Futility of Work
\p \v 18 \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hated|וְשָׂנֵ֤אתִֽי\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb for which|שֶׁאֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb I had toiled|עֲמָלִ֔י\rb*\rb |עָמֵ֖ל\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb because I must leave it|שֶׁ֣אַנִּיחֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb to the man|לָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb who comes|שֶׁיִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb after me|אַחֲרָֽי׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb And who|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb knows|יוֹדֵ֗עַ\rb* \rb whether that man will be|יִהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb wise|הֶֽחָכָ֤ם\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb foolish|סָכָ֔ל\rb*? \rb Yet he will take|וְיִשְׁלַט֙\rb* \rb over all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the labor|עֲמָלִ֔י\rb* \rb at which I have worked|שֶֽׁעָמַ֥לְתִּי\rb* \rb skillfully|וְשֶׁחָכַ֖מְתִּי\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*. \rb This|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb is futile|הָֽבֶל׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb So|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb my heart|לִבִּ֑י\rb* \rb began|וְסַבּ֥וֹתִֽי\rb* \rb to despair|לְיַאֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb over|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the labor|הֶ֣עָמָ֔ל\rb* \rb that I had done|שֶׁעָמַ֖לְתִּי\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb When|כִּי־\rb* \rb there is|יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb a man|אָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb who has labored|שֶׁעֲמָל֛וֹ\rb* \rb with wisdom|בְּחָכְמָ֥ה\rb*, \rb knowledge|וּבְדַ֖עַת\rb*, \rb and skill|וּבְכִשְׁר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and he must give|יִתְּנֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb his portion|חֶלְק֔וֹ\rb* \rb to a man|וּלְאָדָ֞ם\rb* \rb who has not|שֶׁלֹּ֤א\rb* \rb worked|עָֽמַל־\rb* \rb for it|בּוֹ֙\rb*, \rb this|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb is futile|הֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb and a great|רַבָּֽה׃\rb* \rb evil|וְרָעָ֥ה\rb*. \v 22 \rb For|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb what|מֶֽה־\rb* \rb does a man|לָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb get|הֹוֶ֤ה\rb* \rb for all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the toil|עֲמָל֔וֹ\rb*\rb |לִבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and striving|וּבְרַעְי֖וֹן\rb* \rb with which|שֶׁה֥וּא\rb* \rb he labors|עָמֵ֖ל\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*? \v 23 \rb Indeed|כִּ֧י\rb*, \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb his days|יָמָ֣יו\rb* \rb are filled with grief|מַכְאֹבִ֗ים\rb*, \rb and his task|עִנְיָנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb is sorrowful|וָכַ֙עַס֙\rb*; \rb even|גַּם־\rb* \rb at night|בַּלַּ֖יְלָה\rb*, \rb his mind|לִבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb rest|שָׁכַ֣ב\rb*. \rb This|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb is futile|הֶ֥בֶל\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Nothing|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb is better|ט֤וֹב\rb* \rb for a man|בָּאָדָם֙\rb* \rb than to eat|שֶׁיֹּאכַ֣ל\rb* \rb and drink|וְשָׁתָ֔ה\rb* \rb and enjoy|וְהֶרְאָ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |נַפְשׁ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb his work|בַּעֲמָל֑וֹ\rb*. \rb I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb have also|גַּם־\rb* \rb seen|רָאִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb this|זֹה֙\rb* \rb is|הִֽיא׃\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*. \v 25 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb apart from|ח֥וּץ\rb* \rb Him|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb*,\f + \fr 2:25 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, Syriac; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa apart from me \ft or \fqa more than I\f* \rb who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb can eat|יֹאכַ֛ל\rb* \rb and who|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb can find enjoyment|יָח֖וּשׁ\rb*? \v 26 \rb To|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the man|לְאָדָם֙\rb* \rb who is pleasing|שֶׁטּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb in His sight|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb*, \rb He gives|נָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֥ה\rb* \rb and knowledge|וְדַ֖עַת\rb* \rb and joy|וְשִׂמְחָ֑ה\rb*, \rb but to the sinner|וְלַחוֹטֶא֩\rb* \rb He assigns|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb the task|עִנְיָ֜ן\rb* \rb of gathering|לֶאֱס֣וֹף\rb* \rb and accumulating that which|וְלִכְנ֗וֹס\rb* \rb he will hand over|לָתֵת֙\rb* \rb to one who pleases|לְטוֹב֙\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*. \rb This|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb is futile|הֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb and a pursuit|וּרְע֥וּת\rb* \rb of the wind|רֽוּחַ׃\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 To Everything There Is a Season
\q1 \v 1 \rb To everything|לַכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb there is a season|זְמָ֑ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and a time|וְעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb for every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb purpose|חֵ֖פֶץ\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃ס\rb*:
\q1 \v 2 \rb a time|עֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to be born|לָלֶ֖דֶת\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb to die|לָמ֑וּת\rb*,
\q2 \rb a time|עֵ֣ת\rb* \rb to plant|לָטַ֔עַת\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֖ת\rb* \rb to uproot|לַעֲק֥וֹר\rb*\rb |נָטֽוּעַ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 3 \rb a time|עֵ֤ת\rb* \rb to kill|לַהֲרוֹג֙\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb to heal|לִרְפּ֔וֹא\rb*,
\q2 \rb a time|עֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to break down|לִפְר֖וֹץ\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנֽוֹת׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 4 \rb a time|עֵ֤ת\rb* \rb to weep|לִבְכּוֹת֙\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb to laugh|לִשְׂח֔וֹק\rb*,
\q2 \rb a time|עֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to mourn|סְפ֖וֹד\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to dance|רְקֽוֹד׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 5 \rb a time|עֵ֚ת\rb* \rb to cast away|לְהַשְׁלִ֣יךְ\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֖ת\rb* \rb to gather|כְּנ֣וֹס\rb* \rb stones together|אֲבָנִ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb a time|עֵ֣ת\rb* \rb to embrace|לַחֲב֔וֹק\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֖ת\rb* \rb to refrain|לִרְחֹ֥ק\rb* \rb from embracing|מֵחַבֵּֽק׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 6 \rb a time|עֵ֤ת\rb* \rb to search|לְבַקֵּשׁ֙\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb to count as lost|לְאַבֵּ֔ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb a time|עֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to keep|לִשְׁמ֖וֹר\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to discard|לְהַשְׁלִֽיךְ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 7 \rb a time|עֵ֤ת\rb* \rb to tear|לִקְר֙וֹעַ֙\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb to mend|לִתְפּ֔וֹר\rb*,
\q2 \rb a time|עֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to be silent|לַחֲשׁ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּֽר׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 8 \rb a time|עֵ֤ת\rb* \rb to love|לֶֽאֱהֹב֙\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb to hate|לִשְׂנֹ֔א\rb*,
\q2 \rb a time|עֵ֥ת\rb* \rb for war|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb and a time|וְעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb for peace|שָׁלֽוֹם׃ס\rb*.
\s1 God’s Works Remain Forever
\p \v 9 \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb does the worker|הָֽעוֹשֶׂ֔ה\rb*\rb |בַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb gain|יִּתְרוֹן֙\rb* \rb from his|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb toil|עָמֵֽל׃\rb*? \v 10 \rb I have seen|רָאִ֣יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the burden|הָֽעִנְיָ֗ן\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb has laid|נָתַ֧ן\rb* \rb upon the sons|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of men|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb to occupy|לַעֲנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb them|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb He has made|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb everything|הַכֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb beautiful|יָפֶ֣ה\rb* \rb in its time|בְעִתּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb He has also|גַּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb set|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb eternity|הָעֹלָם֙\rb* \rb in the hearts of men|בְּלִבָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb yet|מִבְּלִ֞י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb they|הָאָדָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb cannot|לֹא־\rb* \rb fathom|יִמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb the work|הַֽמַּעֲשֶׂ֛ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb from beginning|מֵרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb end|סֽוֹף׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb I know|יָדַ֕עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb there is nothing|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb better|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb for them|בָּ֑ם\rb* \rb than|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb to rejoice|לִשְׂמ֔וֹחַ\rb* \rb and do|וְלַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb good|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb while they live|בְּחַיָּֽיו׃\rb*, \v 13 \rb and also|וְגַ֤ם\rb* \rb that every|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָם֙\rb* \rb should eat|שֶׁיֹּאכַ֣ל\rb* \rb and drink|וְשָׁתָ֔ה\rb* \rb and find|וְרָאָ֥ה\rb* \rb satisfaction|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb his labor|עֲמָל֑וֹ\rb* — \rb this is|הִֽיא׃\rb* \rb the gift|מַתַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*. \v 14 \rb I know|יָדַ֗עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |ה֚וּא\rb* \rb does|יַעֲשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb endures forever|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֔ם\rb*; \rb nothing|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb can be added|לְהוֹסִ֔יף\rb* \rb to it|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb or taken|לִגְרֹ֑עַ\rb* \rb from it|וּמִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb*.\rb |אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb God|וְהָאֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb does it|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb so that they should fear|שֶׁיִּֽרְא֖וּ\rb* \rb Him|מִלְּפָנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb What exists|מַה־\rb* \rb has already|כְּבָ֣ר\rb*\rb |ה֔וּא\rb* \rb been|שֶּֽׁהָיָה֙\rb*, \rb and what|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb will be|לִהְי֖וֹת\rb* \rb has already|כְּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb been|הָיָ֑ה\rb*, \rb for God|וְהָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb will call to account|יְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb what has passed|נִרְדָּֽף׃\rb*.
\s1 From Dust to Dust
\p \v 16 \rb Furthermore|וְע֥וֹד\rb*, \rb I saw|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb* \rb that in the place|מְק֤וֹם\rb* \rb of judgment|הַמִּשְׁפָּט֙\rb* \rb there is|שָׁ֣מָּה\rb* \rb wickedness|הָרֶ֔שַׁע\rb*, \rb and in the place|וּמְק֥וֹם\rb* \rb of righteousness|הַצֶּ֖דֶק\rb* \rb there is|שָׁ֥מָּה\rb* \rb wickedness|הָרָֽשַׁע׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֤רְתִּֽי\rb* \rb in my heart|בְּלִבִּ֔י\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* “\rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb will judge|יִשְׁפֹּ֖ט\rb* \rb the righteous|הַצַּדִּיק֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the wicked|הָ֣רָשָׁ֔ע\rb*, \rb since|כִּי־\rb* \rb there is a time|עֵ֣ת\rb* \rb for every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb activity|חֵ֔פֶץ\rb*\rb |וְעַ֥ל\rb* \rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb deed|הַֽמַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֤רְתִּֽי\rb* \rb to myself|בְּלִבִּ֔י\rb*, “\rb As for|עַל־\rb*\rb |דִּבְרַת֙\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of men|הָאָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb tests them|לְבָרָ֖ם\rb* \rb so that they may see|וְלִרְא֕וֹת\rb* \rb for themselves|שְׁהֶם־\rb* \rb that they|הֵ֖מָּה\rb*\rb |לָהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb are but beasts|בְּהֵמָ֥ה\rb*.” \v 19 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the fates|מִקְרֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |בְֽנֵי־\rb* \rb of both men|הָאָדָ֜ם\rb* \rb and|וּמִקְרֶ֣ה\rb* \rb beasts|הַבְּהֵמָ֗ה\rb*\rb |וּמִקְרֶ֤ה\rb* \rb are the same|אֶחָד֙\rb*: \rb As one|זֶה֙\rb* \rb dies|כְּמ֥וֹת\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb dies|מ֣וֹת\rb* \rb the other|זֶ֔ה\rb* — \rb they all|לַכֹּ֑ל\rb* \rb have the same|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb breath|וְר֥וּחַ\rb*.\f + \fr 3:19 \ft Or \fqa spirit\f* \rb Man|הָאָדָ֤ם\rb* \rb has no|אָ֔יִן\rb* \rb advantage|וּמוֹתַ֨ר\rb* \rb over|מִן־\rb* \rb the animals|הַבְּהֵמָה֙\rb*, \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb everything|הַכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb is futile|הָֽבֶל׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb All|הַכֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb go|הוֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb place|מָק֣וֹם\rb*; \rb all|הַכֹּל֙\rb* \rb come|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb dust|הֶֽעָפָ֔ר\rb*, \rb and all|וְהַכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb return|שָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb dust|הֶעָפָֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb knows|יוֹדֵ֗עַ\rb* \rb if the spirit|ר֚וּחַ\rb* \rb of man|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הָאָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb rises|הָעֹלָ֥ה\rb*\rb |הִ֖יא\rb* \rb upward|לְמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb and the spirit|וְר֙וּחַ֙\rb* \rb of the animal|הַבְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb descends|הַיֹּרֶ֥דֶת\rb*\rb |הִ֖יא\rb*\rb |לְמַ֥טָּה\rb* \rb into the earth|לָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*? \v 22 \rb I have seen|וְרָאִ֗יתִי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there is nothing|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb better|טוֹב֙\rb* \rb for a man|הָאָדָם֙\rb* \rb than|מֵאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb to enjoy|יִשְׂמַ֤ח\rb* \rb his work|בְּֽמַעֲשָׂ֔יו\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb that|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is his lot|חֶלְק֑וֹ\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb can bring him|יְבִיאֶ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb to see|לִרְא֔וֹת\rb* \rb what|בְּמֶ֖ה\rb* \rb will come|שֶׁיִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb after him|אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*?
\c 4
\s1 The Evil of Oppression
\p \v 1 \rb Again I looked|וְשַׁ֣בְתִּֽי\rb*, \rb and I|אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb considered|וָאֶרְאֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the oppression|הָ֣עֲשֻׁקִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb taking place|נַעֲשִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*. \rb I saw|וְהִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the tears|דִּמְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the oppressed|הָעֲשֻׁקִ֗ים\rb*, \rb and they had no|וְאֵ֤ין\rb* \rb comforter|מְנַחֵ֔ם\rb*; \rb the power lay|כֹּ֔חַ\rb* \rb in the hands|וּמִיַּ֤ד\rb* \rb of their oppressors|עֹֽשְׁקֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb and there was no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb comforter|מְנַחֵֽם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So I|אֲנִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb admired|וְשַׁבֵּ֧חַ\rb* \rb the dead|הַמֵּתִ֖ים\rb*, \rb who had already|שֶׁכְּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb died|מֵ֑תוּ\rb*, \rb above|מִן־\rb* \rb the living|הַ֣חַיִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb*\rb |הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb are still|עֲדֶֽנָה׃\rb* \rb alive|חַיִּ֖ים\rb*. \v 3 \rb But better|וְטוֹב֙\rb* \rb than both|מִשְּׁנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb is he who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb yet|עֲדֶ֖ן\rb* \rb existed|הָיָ֑ה\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb has not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb seen|רָאָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָ֔ע\rb*\rb |הַמַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is done|נַעֲשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb I|אֲנִ֜י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וְרָאִ֨יתִֽי\rb* \rb that all|כָּל־\rb* \rb labor|עָמָ֗ל\rb* \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb success|כִּשְׁר֣וֹן\rb*\rb |הַֽמַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb spring from|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |הִ֥יא\rb* \rb a man’s|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb envy|קִנְאַת־\rb* \rb of his neighbor|מֵרֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb This|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb is futile|הֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb and a pursuit|וּרְע֥וּת\rb* \rb of the wind|רֽוּחַ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb The fool|הַכְּסִיל֙\rb* \rb folds|חֹבֵ֣ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his hands|יָדָ֔יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and consumes|וְאֹכֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his own flesh|בְּשָׂרֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb Better|ט֕וֹב\rb* \rb one handful|מְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |כַ֖ף\rb* \rb with tranquility|נָ֑חַת\rb*
\q2 \rb than two handfuls|מִמְּלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |חָפְנַ֛יִם\rb* \rb with toil|עָמָ֖ל\rb* \rb and pursuit|וּרְע֥וּת\rb* \rb of the wind|רֽוּחַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Again|וְשַׁ֧בְתִּי\rb*, \rb I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb saw|וָאֶרְאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb futility|הֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb There is|יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb a|אֶחָד֩\rb* \rb man all alone|וְאֵ֨ין\rb*\rb |שֵׁנִ֜י\rb*, \rb without|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb even|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb or brother|וָאָ֣ח\rb*. \rb And though there is no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb end|קֵץ֙\rb*\rb |לְכָל־\rb* \rb to his labor|עֲמָל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb his eyes|עֵינָיו\rb* \rb are still|גַּם־\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb content|תִשְׂבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb with his wealth|עֹ֑שֶׁר\rb*: “\rb For whom|וּלְמִ֣י׀\rb* \rb do I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb toil|עָמֵ֗ל\rb* \rb and bereave|וּמְחַסֵּ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my soul|נַפְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb of enjoyment|מִטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb*?” \rb This|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb is futile|הֶ֛בֶל\rb* — \rb a miserable|רָ֖ע\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb task|וְעִנְיַ֥ן\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Two|הַשְּׁנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb are better|טוֹבִ֥ים\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָ֑ד\rb*, \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb they have|יֵשׁ־\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb a good|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb return|שָׂכָ֥ר\rb* \rb for their labor|בַּעֲמָלָֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb falls down|יִפֹּ֔לוּ\rb*, \rb his companion|חֲבֵר֑וֹ\rb* \rb can lift him up|יָקִ֣ים\rb*;\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb but pity|וְאִ֣יל֗וֹ\rb* \rb the one|הָֽאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb who falls|שֶׁיִּפּ֔וֹל\rb* \rb without|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb another|שֵׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb to help him up|לַהֲקִימֽוֹ׃\rb*! \v 11 \rb Again|גַּ֛ם\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb lie down together|יִשְׁכְּב֥וּ\rb*, \rb they will keep warm|וְחַ֣ם\rb*; \rb but how|אֵ֥יךְ\rb* \rb can one|וּלְאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb keep warm alone|יֵחָֽם׃\rb*? \v 12 \rb And though|וְאִֽם־\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb may be overpowered|יִתְקְפוֹ֙\rb*, \rb two|הַשְּׁנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb can resist|יַעַמְד֣וּ\rb*\rb |נֶגְדּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Moreover, a cord|וְהַחוּט֙\rb* \rb of three|הַֽמְשֻׁלָּ֔שׁ\rb* \rb strands is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb quickly|בִמְהֵרָ֖ה\rb* \rb broken|יִנָּתֵֽק׃\rb*.
\s1 The Futility of Power
\p \v 13 \rb Better|ט֛וֹב\rb* \rb is a poor|מִסְכֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb but wise|וְחָכָ֑ם\rb* \rb youth|יֶ֥לֶד\rb* \rb than an old|זָקֵן֙\rb* \rb but foolish|וּכְסִ֔יל\rb* \rb king|מִמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb longer|עֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb knows|יָדַ֥ע\rb* \rb how to take a warning|לְהִזָּהֵ֖ר\rb*. \v 14 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the youth has come|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb from the prison|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |הָסוּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to the kingship|לִמְלֹ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb though|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |גַּ֥ם\rb* \rb he was born|נוֹלַ֥ד\rb* \rb poor|רָֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb in his own kingdom|בְּמַלְכוּת֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb I saw that|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who lived|הַ֣חַיִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and walked|הַֽמְהַלְּכִ֖ים\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb* \rb followed|עִ֚ם\rb* \rb this second one|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb*, \rb the youth|הַיֶּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb succeeded|יַעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb the king|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb There is no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb limit|קֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb*\rb |לְכֹ֤ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb before them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Yet|גַּ֥ם\rb* \rb the successor|ב֑וֹ\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be celebrated|יִשְׂמְחוּ־\rb* \rb by those who come even later|הָאַחֲרוֹנִ֖ים\rb*. \rb This|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb too|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb* \rb is futile|הֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb and a pursuit|וְרַעְי֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the wind|רֽוּחַ׃\rb*.
\c 5
\s1 Approaching God with Fear
\p \v 1 \rb Guard|שְׁמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb your steps|רַגְלֶיךָ\rb* \rb when|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you go|תֵּלֵךְ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*. \rb Draw near|וְקָר֣וֹב\rb* \rb to listen|לִשְׁמֹ֔עַ\rb* \rb rather than to offer|מִתֵּ֥ת\rb* \rb the sacrifice|זָ֑בַח\rb* \rb of fools|הַכְּסִילִ֖ים\rb*, \rb who|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb do not|אֵינָ֥ם\rb* \rb know that|יוֹדְעִ֖ים\rb* \rb they do|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb wrong|רָֽע׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be quick|תְּבַהֵ֨ל\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb speak|פִּ֜יךָ\rb*, \rb and do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be hasty|יְמַהֵ֛ר\rb* \rb in your heart|וְלִבְּךָ֧\rb* \rb to utter|לְהוֹצִ֥יא\rb* \rb a word|דָבָ֖ר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֤ים\rb* \rb is in heaven|בַּשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are on|עַל־\rb* \rb earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*. \rb So|עַֽל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb let your words|דְבָרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb be|יִהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb few|מְעַטִּֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb As|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb a dream|הַחֲל֖וֹם\rb* \rb comes|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb through many|בְּרֹ֣ב\rb* \rb cares|עִנְיָ֑ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb so the speech|וְק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of a fool|כְּסִ֖יל\rb* \rb comes with many|בְּרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb words|דְּבָרִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb you make|תִּדֹּ֨ר\rb* \rb a vow|נֶ֜דֶר\rb* \rb to God|לֵֽאלֹהִ֗ים\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb delay|תְּאַחֵר֙\rb* \rb in fulfilling it|לְשַׁלְּמ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb He takes no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb pleasure|חֵ֖פֶץ\rb* \rb in fools|בַּכְּסִילִ֑ים\rb*.\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb Fulfill|שַׁלֵּֽם׃\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your vow|תִּדֹּ֖ר\rb*. \v 5 \rb It is better|ט֖וֹב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to vow|תִדֹּ֑ר\rb* \rb than to make a vow|מִשֶׁתִּדּ֖וֹר\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb fulfill it|תְשַׁלֵּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let|תִּתֵּ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your mouth|פִּ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb cause your flesh|בְּשָׂרֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb to sin|לַחֲטִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb tell|תֹּאמַר֙\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the messenger|הַמַּלְאָ֔ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 5:6 \ft Or \fqa angel\f* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb your vow|הִ֑יא\rb* \rb was a mistake|שְׁגָגָ֖ה\rb*. \rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb should God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb be angry|יִקְצֹ֤ף\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb your words|קוֹלֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and destroy|וְחִבֵּ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of your hands|יָדֶֽיךָ׃\rb*? \v 7 \rb For as|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb many|בְרֹ֤ב\rb* \rb dreams|חֲלֹמוֹת֙\rb* \rb bring futility|וַהֲבָלִ֔ים\rb*, \rb so do many|הַרְבֵּ֑ה\rb* \rb words|וּדְבָרִ֖ים\rb*. \rb Therefore|כִּ֥י\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb fear|יְרָֽא׃\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*.
\s1 The Futility of Wealth
\r (\ref Psalm 49:1–20|PSA 49:1-20\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you see|תִּרְאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the oppression|עֹ֣שֶׁק\rb* \rb of the poor|רָ֠שׁ\rb* \rb and the denial|וְגֵ֨זֶל\rb* \rb of justice|מִשְׁפָּ֤ט\rb* \rb and righteousness|וָצֶ֙דֶק֙\rb* \rb in the province|בַמְּדִינָ֔ה\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be astonished|תִּתְמַ֖הּ\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the matter|הַחֵ֑פֶץ\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb one official|גָבֹ֜הַּ\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֤ל\rb* \rb is watched by|שֹׁמֵ֔ר\rb* \rb a superior|גָּבֹ֙הַ֙\rb*, \rb and others higher still|וּגְבֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb are over them|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb The produce|וְיִתְר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the earth|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb is taken by all|בַּכֹּ֣ל\rb*;\rb |הִיא\rb* \rb the king himself|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb profits|נֶעֱבָֽד׃\rb* \rb from the fields|לְשָׂדֶ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb He who loves|אֹהֵ֥ב\rb* \rb money|כֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb is never|לֹא־\rb* \rb satisfied|יִשְׂבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb by money|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*, \rb and he who|וּמִֽי־\rb* \rb loves|אֹהֵ֥ב\rb* \rb wealth|בֶּהָמ֖וֹן\rb* \rb is never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb satisfied by income|תְבוּאָ֑ה\rb*. \rb This|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb is futile|הָֽבֶל׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb When good things|הַטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb increase|בִּרְבוֹת֙\rb*, \rb so do|רַבּ֖וּ\rb* \rb those who consume them|אוֹכְלֶ֑יהָ\rb*; \rb what then|וּמַה־\rb* \rb is the profit|כִּשְׁרוֹן֙\rb* \rb to the owner|לִבְעָלֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb except|כִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb to behold them|רְאִיַּת\rb* \rb with his eyes|עֵינָֽיו׃\rb*?
\p \v 12 \rb The sleep|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the worker|הָעֹבֵ֔ד\rb* \rb is sweet|מְתוּקָה֙\rb*, \rb whether|אִם־\rb* \rb he eats|יֹאכֵ֑ל\rb* \rb little|מְעַ֥ט\rb* \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb much|הַרְבֵּ֖ה\rb*, \rb but the abundance|וְהַשָּׂבָע֙\rb* \rb of the rich man|לֶֽעָשִׁ֔יר\rb* \rb permits|מַנִּ֥יחַֽ\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb no|אֵינֶ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb sleep|לִישֽׁוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb There is|יֵ֚שׁ\rb* \rb a grievous|חוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb evil|רָעָ֣ה\rb* \rb I have seen|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*: \rb wealth|עֹ֛שֶׁר\rb* \rb hoarded|שָׁמ֥וּר\rb* \rb to the harm|לְרָעָתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb of its owner|לִבְעָלָ֖יו\rb*, \v 14 \rb or|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb wealth|הָעֹ֥שֶׁר\rb* \rb lost|וְאָבַ֛ד\rb* \rb in a failed|רָ֑ע\rb* \rb venture|בְּעִנְיַ֣ן\rb*, \rb so when that man has|וְהוֹלִ֣יד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb there is nothing|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb to pass on|בְּיָד֖וֹ\rb*\rb |מְאֽוּמָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb As|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb a man came|יָצָא֙\rb* \rb from his mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb womb|מִבֶּ֣טֶן\rb*, \rb so he will depart|לָלֶ֖כֶת\rb* \rb again|יָשׁ֥וּב\rb*, \rb naked|עָר֛וֹם\rb* \rb as he arrived|כְּשֶׁבָּ֑א\rb*. \rb He takes|יִשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb nothing|וּמְא֙וּמָה֙\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb for his labor|בַעֲמָל֔וֹ\rb* \rb to carry|שֶׁיֹּלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in his hands|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb This|זֹה֙\rb* \rb too|וְגַם־\rb* \rb is a grievous|חוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb affliction|רָעָ֣ה\rb*: \rb Exactly as|כָּל־\rb*\rb |עֻמַּ֥ת\rb* \rb a man is born|שֶׁבָּ֖א\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb he will depart|יֵלֵ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb What|וּמַה־\rb* \rb does he gain|יִּתְר֣וֹן\rb* \rb as he toils|שֶֽׁיַּעֲמֹ֖ל\rb* \rb for the wind|לָרֽוּחַ׃\rb*? \v 17 \rb Moreover|גַּ֥ם\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his days|יָמָ֖יו\rb* \rb he eats|יֹאכֵ֑ל\rb* \rb in darkness|בַּחֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb*, \rb with much|הַרְבֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb sorrow|וְכָעַ֥ס\rb*, \rb sickness|וְחָלְי֥וֹ\rb*, \rb and anger|וָקָֽצֶף׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Here|הִנֵּ֞ה\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אָ֗נִי\rb* \rb have seen|רָאִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb to be good|ט֣וֹב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb and fitting|יָפֶ֣ה\rb*: \rb to eat|לֶֽאֶכוֹל־\rb* \rb and drink|וְ֠לִשְׁתּוֹת\rb*, \rb and to find|וְלִרְא֨וֹת\rb* \rb satisfaction|טוֹבָ֜ה\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the labor|עֲמָל֣וֹ׀\rb* \rb one does|שֶׁיַּעֲמֹ֣ל\rb* \rb under|תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb the sun|הַשֶּׁ֗מֶשׁ\rb* \rb during the few|מִסְפַּ֧ר\rb* \rb days|יְמֵי־\rb* \rb of life|חַיָּו\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb has given|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb him|ל֥וֹ\rb* — \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb this|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is his lot|חֶלְקֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Furthermore|גַּ֣ם\rb*, \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִים֩\rb* \rb has given|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb riches|עֹ֨שֶׁר\rb* \rb and wealth|וּנְכָסִ֜ים\rb* \rb to|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb every|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֡ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*, \rb and He has enabled him|וְהִשְׁלִיט֨וֹ\rb* \rb to enjoy them|לֶאֱכֹ֤ל\rb*,\rb |מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb to accept|וְלָשֵׂ֣את\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his lot|חֶלְק֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and to rejoice|וְלִשְׂמֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb in his labor|בַּעֲמָל֑וֹ\rb*. \rb This|זֹ֕ה\rb* \rb is a gift|מַתַּ֥ת\rb* \rb from God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*.\rb |הִֽיא׃\rb* \v 20 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb a man seldom|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |הַרְבֵּ֔ה\rb* \rb considers|יִזְכֹּ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his life|חַיָּ֑יו\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb keeps him occupied|מַעֲנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb with the joy|בְּשִׂמְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb of his heart|לִבּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\c 6
\s1 The Futility of Life
\p \v 1 \rb There is|יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb another evil|רָעָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have seen|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and it|הִ֖יא\rb* \rb weighs heavily|וְרַבָּ֥ה\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb mankind|הָאָדָֽם׃\rb*: \v 2 \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֡ים\rb* \rb gives|יִתֶּן־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb riches|עֹשֶׁר֩\rb*, \rb wealth|וּנְכָסִ֨ים\rb*, \rb and honor|וְכָב֜וֹד\rb*, \rb so that he lacks|חָסֵ֥ר\rb* \rb nothing|וְֽאֵינֶ֨נּוּ\rb* \rb his heart|לְנַפְשׁ֣וֹ׀\rb*\rb |מִכֹּ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb desires|יִתְאַוֶּ֗ה\rb*; \rb but God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb does not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb allow him|יַשְׁלִיטֶ֤נּוּ\rb* \rb to enjoy them|לֶאֱכֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb*. \rb Instead|כִּ֛י\rb*, \rb a stranger|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |נָכְרִ֖י\rb* \rb will enjoy them|יֹֽאכֲלֶ֑נּוּ\rb*. \rb This|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb is futile|הֶ֛בֶל\rb* \rb and a grievous|וָחֳלִ֥י\rb* \rb affliction|רָ֖ע\rb*.\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb |אִם־\rb* \rb A man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb may father|יוֹלִ֣יד\rb* \rb a hundred children|מֵאָ֡ה\rb* \rb and live|יִֽחְיֶ֜ה\rb* \rb for many|רַבּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb years|וְשָׁנִים֩\rb*; \rb yet no matter how long|וְרַ֣ב׀\rb*\rb |שֶׁיִּהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb he lives|יְמֵֽי־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֗יו\rb*, \rb if he|וְנַפְשׁוֹ֙\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb is unsatisfied|תִשְׂבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb with|מִן־\rb* \rb his prosperity|הַטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb and does not|לֹא־\rb*\rb |הָ֣יְתָה\rb* \rb even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb receive a proper burial|קְבוּרָ֖ה\rb*, \rb I say|אָמַ֕רְתִּי\rb* \rb that a stillborn child|הַנָּֽפֶל׃\rb* \rb is better off|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb than he|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb*. \v 4 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a stillborn child enters|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb in futility|בַהֶ֥בֶל\rb* \rb and departs|יֵלֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb in darkness|וּבַחֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb*, \rb and his name|שְׁמ֥וֹ\rb* \rb is shrouded|יְכֻסֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb in obscurity|וּבַחֹ֖שֶׁךְ\rb*. \v 5 \rb The child|לָזֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb though|גַּם־\rb* \rb neither|לֹא־\rb* \rb seeing|רָאָ֖ה\rb* \rb the sun|שֶׁ֥מֶשׁ\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb knowing anything|יָדָ֑ע\rb*, \rb has more rest|נַ֥חַת\rb* \rb than that man|מִזֶּֽה׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb even if|וְאִלּ֣וּ\rb* \rb he lives|חָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb a thousand|אֶ֤לֶף\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִים֙\rb* \rb twice over|פַּעֲמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb but fails to|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb enjoy|רָאָ֑ה\rb* \rb his prosperity|וְטוֹבָ֖ה\rb*. \rb Do not|הֲלֹ֛א\rb* \rb all|הַכֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb go|הוֹלֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the same|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb place|מָק֥וֹם\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb a man’s|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb labor|עֲמַ֥ל\rb* \rb is for his mouth|לְפִ֑יהוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb yet|וְגַם־\rb* \rb his appetite|הַנֶּ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb is never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb satisfied|תִמָּלֵֽא׃\rb*.\f + \fr 6:7 \ft Hebrew \fqa filled\f*
\p \v 8 \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb advantage|יּוֹתֵ֥ר\rb*, \rb then|כִּ֛י\rb*, \rb has the wise man|לֶחָכָ֖ם\rb* \rb over|מִֽן־\rb* \rb the fool|הַכְּסִ֑יל\rb*? \rb What gain comes|מַה־\rb* \rb to the poor man|לֶּעָנִ֣י\rb* \rb who knows|יוֹדֵ֔עַ\rb* \rb how to conduct himself|לַהֲלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb before|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb others|הַחַיִּֽים׃\rb*? \v 9 \rb Better|ט֛וֹב\rb* \rb what the eye|עֵינַ֖יִם\rb* \rb can see|מַרְאֵ֥ה\rb* \rb than the wandering|מֵֽהֲלָךְ־\rb* \rb of desire|נָ֑פֶשׁ\rb*. \rb This|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb is futile|הֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb and a pursuit|וּרְע֥וּת\rb* \rb of the wind|רֽוּחַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Whatever|מַה־\rb* \rb exists|שֶּֽׁהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb was named|נִקְרָ֣א\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb long ago|כְּבָר֙\rb*, \rb and it is known|וְנוֹדָ֖ע\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb man is|אָדָ֑ם\rb*; \rb but he|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb cannot|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֣ל\rb* \rb contend|לָדִ֔ין\rb* \rb with|עִ֥ם\rb* \rb one stronger|שֶׁהַתְקִיף\rb* \rb than he|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |יֵשׁ־\rb* \rb the more|הַרְבֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb words|דְּבָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb the more|מַרְבִּ֣ים\rb* \rb futility|הָ֑בֶל\rb* — \rb and how|מַה־\rb* \rb does that profit|יֹּתֵ֖ר\rb* \rb anyone|לָאָדָֽם׃\rb*? \v 12 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb knows|יוֹדֵעַ֩\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb is good|טּ֨וֹב\rb* \rb for a man|לָֽאָדָ֜ם\rb*\rb |בַּֽחַיִּ֗ים\rb* \rb during the few|מִסְפַּ֛ר\rb* \rb days in which|יְמֵי־\rb* \rb he passes through|וְיַעֲשֵׂ֣ם\rb* \rb his fleeting|הֶבְל֖וֹ\rb* \rb life|חַיֵּ֥י\rb* \rb like a shadow|כַּצֵּ֑ל\rb*?\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb can tell|יַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb a man|לָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb will come|יִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb after him|אַחֲרָ֖יו\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*?
\c 7
\s1 The Value of Wisdom
\q1 \v 1 \rb A good name|שֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb is better|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb than fine|ט֑וֹב\rb* \rb perfume|מִשֶּׁ֣מֶן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and one’s day|וְי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of death|הַמָּ֔וֶת\rb* \rb is better than his day|מִיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb of birth|הִוָּלְדֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb It is better|ט֞וֹב\rb* \rb to enter|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb a house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of mourning|אֵ֗בֶל\rb*
\q2 \rb than|מִלֶּ֙כֶת֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb a house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of feasting|מִשְׁתֶּ֔ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb since|בַּאֲשֶׁ֕ר\rb* \rb death|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is the end|ס֣וֹף\rb* \rb of every|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the living|וְהַחַ֖י\rb* \rb should take this|יִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb heart|לִבּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Sorrow|כַּ֖עַס\rb* \rb is better|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb than laughter|מִשְּׂחֹ֑ק\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a sad|בְרֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb countenance|פָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb is good|יִ֥יטַב\rb* \rb for the heart|לֵֽב׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb The heart|לֵ֤ב\rb* \rb of the wise|חֲכָמִים֙\rb* \rb is in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of mourning|אֵ֔בֶל\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the heart|וְלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb of fools|כְּסִילִ֖ים\rb* \rb is in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of pleasure|שִׂמְחָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb It is better|ט֕וֹב\rb* \rb to heed|לִשְׁמֹ֖עַ\rb* \rb a wise man’s|חָכָ֑ם\rb* \rb rebuke|גַּעֲרַ֣ת\rb*
\q2 \rb than|מֵאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb to listen|שֹׁמֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb to the song|שִׁ֥יר\rb* \rb of fools|כְּסִילִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb like the crackling|כְק֤וֹל\rb* \rb of thorns|הַסִּירִים֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the pot|הַסִּ֔יר\rb*,
\q2 \rb so|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb is the laughter|שְׂחֹ֣ק\rb* \rb of the fool|הַכְּסִ֑יל\rb*. \rb This|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb too|וְגַם־\rb* \rb is futile|הָֽבֶל׃\rb*.
\b 
