\q1 \v 20 \rb Surely|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb righteous|צַדִּ֖יק\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb on earth|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb does|יַעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb good|טּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb and never|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb sins|יֶחֱטָֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb |גַּ֤ם\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb pay|תִּתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb attention|לִבֶּ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb to every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb word|הַדְּבָרִים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is spoken|יְדַבֵּ֔רוּ\rb*, \rb or|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb you may hear|תִשְׁמַ֥ע\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb cursing you|מְקַלְלֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb you know|יָדַ֣ע\rb* \rb in your heart|לִבֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb many|רַבּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb you yourself|אַתְּ\rb* \rb have cursed|קִלַּ֥לְתָּ\rb* \rb others|אֲחֵרִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֖ה\rb* \rb I tested|נִסִּ֣יתִי\rb* \rb by wisdom, saying|בַֽחָכְמָ֑ה\rb*, “\rb I resolve|אָמַ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb to be wise|אֶחְכָּ֔מָה\rb*.” \rb But it|וְהִ֖יא\rb* \rb was beyond|רְחוֹקָ֥ה\rb* \rb me|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb exists|שֶּׁהָיָ֑ה\rb* \rb is out of reach|רָח֖וֹק\rb* \rb and very deep|וְעָמֹ֥ק׀\rb*\rb |עָמֹ֖ק\rb*. \rb Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb can fathom it|יִמְצָאֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*?
\p \v 25 \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb directed|סַבּ֨וֹתִֽי\rb* \rb my mind|וְלִבִּי֙\rb* \rb to understand|לָדַ֣עַת\rb*, \rb to explore|וְלָת֔וּר\rb*, \rb to search out|וּבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb and explanations|וְחֶשְׁבּ֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and to understand|וְלָדַ֙עַת֙\rb* \rb the stupidity|כֶּ֔סֶל\rb* \rb of wickedness|רֶ֣שַׁע\rb* \rb and the folly|וְהַסִּכְל֖וּת\rb* \rb of madness|הוֹלֵלֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb And I|אֲנִ֜י\rb* \rb find|וּמוֹצֶ֨א\rb* \rb more bitter|מַ֣ר\rb* \rb than death|מִמָּ֗וֶת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הִ֨יא\rb* \rb is a snare|מְצוֹדִ֧ים\rb*, \rb whose heart|לִבָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb is a net|וַחֲרָמִ֛ים\rb*, \rb and whose hands|יָדֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb are chains|אֲסוּרִ֣ים\rb*. \rb The man who pleases|ט֞וֹב\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb escapes|יִמָּלֵ֣ט\rb* \rb her|מִמֶּ֔נָּה\rb*, \rb but the sinner|וְחוֹטֵ֖א\rb* \rb is ensnared|יִלָּ֥כֶד\rb*.
\p \v 27 “\rb Behold|רְאֵה֙\rb*,” \rb says|אָמְרָ֖ה\rb* \rb the Teacher|קֹהֶ֑לֶת\rb*, “\rb I have discovered|מָצָ֔אתִי\rb* \rb this|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb by adding one|אַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb thing to another|לְאַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb to find|לִמְצֹ֥א\rb* \rb an explanation|חֶשְׁבּֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb While|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb my soul|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb was still|עוֹד־\rb* \rb searching|בִּקְשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb but not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb finding|מָצָ֑אתִי\rb*, \rb among a thousand|מֵאֶ֙לֶף֙\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֔אתִי\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֤ד\rb* \rb upright man|אָדָ֞ם\rb*, \rb but among all|בְכָל־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb I have not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb found|מָצָֽאתִי׃\rb* \rb one such woman|וְאִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*. \v 29 \rb Only|לְבַד֙\rb* \rb this|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb have I found|רְאֵה־\rb*: \rb I have discovered|מָצָ֔אתִי\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|עָשָׂ֧ה\rb* \rb mankind|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb upright|יָשָׁ֑ר\rb*, \rb but they|וְהֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb have sought out|בִקְשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb many|רַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb schemes|חִשְּׁבֹנ֥וֹת\rb*.”
\c 8
\s1 Obey the King
\q1 
\p \v 1 \rb Who|מִ֚י\rb* \rb is like the wise man|כְּהֶ֣חָכָ֔ם\rb*? \rb Who|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb knows|יוֹדֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb the interpretation|פֵּ֣שֶׁר\rb* \rb of a matter|דָּבָ֑ר\rb*? \rb A man’s|אָדָם֙\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמַ֤ת\rb* \rb brightens|תָּאִ֣יר\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and the sternness|וְעֹ֥ז\rb* \rb of his face|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb is changed|יְשֻׁנֶּֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Keep|שְׁמ֔וֹר\rb* \rb the king’s|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb command|פִּי־\rb*, \rb I say|אֲנִי֙\rb*, \rb because of|וְעַ֕ל\rb*\rb |דִּבְרַ֖ת\rb* \rb your oath|שְׁבוּעַ֥ת\rb* \rb before God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb hasten|תִּבָּהֵ֤ל\rb* \rb to leave|תֵּלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb his presence|מִפָּנָיו֙\rb*, \rb and do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb persist|תַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb in a bad|רָ֑ע\rb* \rb cause|בְּדָבָ֣ר\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb he will do|יַעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \rb whatever|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he pleases|יַחְפֹּ֖ץ\rb*. \v 4 \rb For|בַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the king’s|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb is supreme|שִׁלְט֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and who|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb can say|יֹֽאמַר־\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*, “\rb What|מַֽה־\rb* \rb are you doing|תַּעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 5 \rb Whoever keeps|שׁוֹמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb his command|מִצְוָ֔ה\rb* \rb will come to|יֵדַ֖ע\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb harm|רָ֑ע\rb*, \rb and a wise|חָכָֽם׃\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֥ב\rb* \rb knows|יֵדַ֖ע\rb* \rb the right time|וְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb and procedure|וּמִשְׁפָּ֔ט\rb*. \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there is|יֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb a right time|עֵ֣ת\rb* \rb and procedure|וּמִשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb* \rb to every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb purpose|חֵ֔פֶץ\rb*, \rb though|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man’s|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb misery|רָעַ֥ת\rb* \rb weighs heavily|רַבָּ֥ה\rb* \rb upon him|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb no one|אֵינֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb knows|יֹדֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb will happen|שֶּׁיִּֽהְיֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb who|מִ֖י\rb* \rb can tell|יַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*\rb |כִּ֚י\rb* \rb what|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is to come|יִֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb*?
\p \v 8 \rb As no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֞ם\rb* \rb has power|שַׁלִּ֤יט\rb* \rb over the wind|בָּר֙וּחַ֙\rb* \rb to contain|לִכְל֣וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הָר֔וּחַ\rb*, \rb so no one|וְאֵ֤ין\rb* \rb has authority|שִׁלְטוֹן֙\rb* \rb over his day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of death|הַמָּ֔וֶת\rb*. \rb As no one|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb can be discharged|מִשְׁלַ֖חַת\rb* \rb in wartime|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*, \rb so wickedness|רֶ֖שַׁע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb release|יְמַלֵּ֥ט\rb* \rb those who practice it|בְּעָלָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb I have seen|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb*, \rb applying|וְנָת֣וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my mind|לִבִּ֔י\rb* \rb to every|לְכָֽל־\rb* \rb deed|מַעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is done|נַעֲשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*; \rb there is a time|עֵ֗ת\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb one man|הָאָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb lords it|שָׁלַ֧ט\rb* \rb over another|בְּאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb to his own detriment|לְרַ֥ע\rb*.
\s1 Fear God
\r (\ref Isaiah 8:11–15|ISA 8:11-15\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb Then too|וּבְכֵ֡ן\rb*, \rb I saw|רָאִיתִי֩\rb* \rb the burial|קְבֻרִ֜ים\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֨ים\rb* \rb who used to go in|וָבָ֗אוּ\rb* \rb and out|יְהַלֵּ֔כוּ\rb* \rb of the holy|קָדוֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb place|וּמִמְּק֤וֹם\rb*, \rb and they were praised|וְיִֽשְׁתַּכְּח֥וּ\rb*\f + \fr 8:10 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Vulgate; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa were soon forgotten\f* \rb in the city|בָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had done|עָשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb so|כֵּן־\rb*. \rb This|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb is futile|הָֽבֶל׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb When|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the sentence|פִתְגָ֔ם\rb* \rb for a crime|הָרָעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb is not|אֵין־\rb* \rb speedily|מְהֵרָ֑ה\rb* \rb executed|נַעֲשָׂ֣ה\rb*,\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֡ן\rb* \rb the hearts|לֵ֧ב\rb*\rb |בְּֽנֵי־\rb* \rb of men|הָאָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb become fully set|מָלֵ֞א\rb* \rb on doing|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb evil|רָֽע׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Although|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb a sinner|חֹטֶ֗א\rb* \rb does|עֹשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb evil|רָ֛ע\rb* \rb a hundred times|מְאַ֖ת\rb* \rb and still lives long|וּמַאֲרִ֣יךְ\rb*, \rb yet|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb know|יוֹדֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb it will go|יִהְיֶה־\rb* \rb well|טּוֹב֙\rb* \rb with those who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb fear|יִֽירְא֖וּ\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb who are reverent|לְיִרְאֵ֣י\rb* \rb in His presence|מִלְּפָנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Yet because|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the wicked do not|אֵינֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb fear|יָרֵ֖א\rb*\rb |מִלִּפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*, \rb it will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb well|וְטוֹב֙\rb* \rb with them|לָֽרָשָׁ֔ע\rb*, \rb and their days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb lengthen|יַאֲרִ֥יךְ\rb* \rb like a shadow|כַּצֵּ֑ל\rb*.
\s1 God’s Ways Are Mysterious
\p \v 14 \rb There is|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb a futility|הֶבֶל֮\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is done|נַעֲשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָרֶץ֒\rb*: \rb There are|יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb righteous men|צַדִּיקִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb get|מַגִּ֤יעַ\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb what the actions|כְּמַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of the wicked deserve|הָרְשָׁעִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and there are|וְיֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb wicked men|רְשָׁעִ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲלֵהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb get|שֶׁמַּגִּ֥יעַ\rb* \rb what the actions|כְּמַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of the righteous deserve|הַצַּדִּיקִ֑ים\rb*. \rb I say|אָמַ֕רְתִּי\rb* \rb that this|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb too|שֶׁגַּם־\rb* \rb is futile|הָֽבֶל׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb So I|אֲנִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commended|וְשִׁבַּ֤חְתִּֽי\rb* \rb the enjoyment of life|הַשִּׂמְחָ֔ה\rb*, \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb there is nothing|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb better|ט֤וֹב\rb* \rb for a man|לָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb than|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכ֥וֹל\rb* \rb and drink|וְלִשְׁתּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and be merry|וְלִשְׂמ֑וֹחַ\rb*. \rb For this joy|וְה֞וּא\rb* \rb will accompany him|יִלְוֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb in his labor|בַעֲמָל֗וֹ\rb* \rb during the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his life|חַיָּ֛יו\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb gives|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb him|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I applied|נָתַ֤תִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my mind|לִבִּי֙\rb* \rb to know|לָדַ֣עַת\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and to observe|וְלִרְאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the task|הָ֣עִנְיָ֔ן\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb one performs|נַעֲשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* — \rb though|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |גַ֤ם\rb* \rb his eyes|בְּעֵינָ֖יו\rb* \rb do not|אֵינֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶֽה׃\rb* \rb sleep|שֵׁנָ֕ה\rb* \rb in the day|בַּיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb or even in the night|וּבַלַּ֔יְלָה\rb* — \v 17 \rb I saw|וְרָאִיתִי֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb work|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִים֒\rb*, \rb and that|כִּי֩\rb* \rb a man|הָאָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb is unable|לֹ֨א\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֜ל\rb* \rb to comprehend|לִמְצוֹא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the work|הַֽמַּעֲשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is done|נַעֲשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb under|תַֽחַת־\rb* \rb the sun|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb*. \rb Despite|בְּ֠שֶׁל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb his|הָאָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb efforts|יַעֲמֹ֧ל\rb* \rb to search it out|לְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb*, \rb he cannot|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb find its meaning|יִמְצָ֑א\rb*; \rb even|וְגַ֨ם\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb the wise|הֶֽחָכָם֙\rb* \rb man claims|יֹאמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to know|לָדַ֔עַת\rb*, \rb he is unable|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb to comprehend|לִמְצֹֽא׃\rb*.
\c 9
\s1 Death Comes to Good and Bad
\p \v 1 \rb So|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I took|נָתַ֤תִּי\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|זֶ֞ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb heart|לִבִּי֙\rb* \rb and concluded|וְלָב֣וּר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |זֶ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the righteous|הַצַּדִּיקִ֧ים\rb* \rb and the wise|וְהַחֲכָמִ֛ים\rb*, \rb as well as their deeds|וַעֲבָדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb are in God’s|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb hands|בְּיַ֣ד\rb*. \rb Man|הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb does not|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb know|יוֹדֵ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb what|הַכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb lies ahead|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*, \rb whether|גַּֽם־\rb* \rb love|אַהֲבָ֣ה\rb* \rb or|גַם־\rb* \rb hate|שִׂנְאָ֗ה\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb |הַכֹּ֞ל\rb* \rb It is the same|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb for all|לַכֹּ֗ל\rb*: \rb There is a common|אֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb fate|מִקְרֶ֨ה\rb* \rb for the righteous|לַצַּדִּ֤יק\rb* \rb and the wicked|וְלָרָשָׁע֙\rb*, \rb for the good and the bad|לַטּוֹב֙\rb*,\f + \fr 9:2 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; Hebrew does not include \fqa and the bad\ft .\f* \rb for the clean|וְלַטָּה֣וֹר\rb* \rb and the unclean|וְלַטָּמֵ֔א\rb*, \rb for the one who sacrifices|וְלַזֹּבֵ֔חַ\rb* \rb and the one|וְלַאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb who does not|אֵינֶ֣נּוּ\rb*\rb |זֹבֵ֑חַ\rb*. \rb As it is for the good|כַּטּוֹב֙\rb*, \rb so it is for the sinner|כַּֽחֹטֶ֔א\rb*; \rb as it is for the one who makes a vow|הַנִּשְׁבָּ֕ע\rb*, \rb so it is|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb for the one who refuses|יָרֵֽא׃\rb* \rb to take a vow|שְׁבוּעָ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb This|זֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb is an evil|רָ֗ע\rb* \rb in everything|בְּכֹ֤ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb is done|נַעֲשָׂה֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb*:\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb There is one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb fate|מִקְרֶ֥ה\rb* \rb for everyone|לַכֹּ֑ל\rb*. \rb Furthermore|וְגַ֣ם\rb*, \rb the hearts|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb of men|בְּֽנֵי־\rb*\rb |הָ֠אָדָם\rb* \rb are full of|מָלֵא־\rb* \rb evil|רָ֨ע\rb* \rb and madness|וְהוֹלֵל֤וֹת\rb*\rb |בִּלְבָבָם֙\rb* \rb while they are alive|בְּחַיֵּיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and afterward|וְאַחֲרָ֖יו\rb* \rb they join|אֶל־\rb* \rb the dead|הַמֵּתִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb There is|יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb hope|בִּטָּח֑וֹן\rb*, \rb however|כִּי־\rb*, \rb for anyone who|מִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is among|יִבָּחֵר\rb*\rb |אֶ֥ל\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb the living|הַחַיִּ֖ים\rb*; \rb for even|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a live|חַי֙\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb dog|לְכֶ֤לֶב\rb* \rb is better|ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb a dead|הַמֵּֽת׃\rb* \rb lion|הָאַרְיֵ֖ה\rb*. \v 5 \rb For|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb the living|הַֽחַיִּ֛ים\rb* \rb know|יוֹדְעִ֖ים\rb* \rb that they will die|שֶׁיָּמֻ֑תוּ\rb*, \rb but the dead|וְהַמֵּתִ֞ים\rb* \rb know|יוֹדְעִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֵינָ֧ם\rb* \rb nothing|מְא֗וּמָה\rb*. \rb They have no|וְאֵֽין־\rb* \rb further|ע֤וֹד\rb* \rb reward|שָׂכָ֔ר\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the memory|זִכְרָֽם׃\rb* \rb of them is forgotten|נִשְׁכַּ֖ח\rb*. \v 6 \rb Their love|אַהֲבָתָ֧ם\rb*,\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb their hate|שִׂנְאָתָ֛ם\rb*,\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb and|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb their envy|קִנְאָתָ֖ם\rb* \rb have already|כְּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb vanished|אָבָ֑דָה\rb*, \rb and they will never again have|אֵין־\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb a share|וְחֵ֨לֶק\rb* \rb in all|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb is done|נַעֲשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\s1 Enjoy Your Portion in This Life
\q1 
\p \v 7 \rb Go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb*, \rb eat|אֱכֹ֤ל\rb* \rb your bread|לַחְמֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb with joy|בְּשִׂמְחָה֙\rb*, \rb and drink|וּֽשֲׁתֵ֥ה\rb* \rb your wine|יֵינֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb with a cheerful|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb heart|בְלֶב־\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb has already|כְבָ֔ר\rb* \rb approved|רָצָ֥ה\rb* \rb your works|מַעֲשֶֽׂיךָ׃\rb*:
\q1 \v 8 \rb Let your garments|בְגָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb always|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |עֵ֕ת\rb* \rb be|יִהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb white|לְבָנִ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and never|אַל־\rb* \rb spare|יֶחְסָֽר׃\rb* \rb the oil|וְשֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb your head|רֹאשְׁךָ֥\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Enjoy|רְאֵ֨ה\rb* \rb life|חַיִּ֜ים\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb your beloved|אָהַ֗בְתָּ\rb* \rb wife|אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵי֙\rb* \rb of the fleeting|הֶבְלֶ֔ךָ\rb*\f + \fr 9:9 \ft Or \fqa futile\ft ; twice in this verse\f* \rb life|חַיֵּ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb God has given|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* — \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb your fleeting|הֶבְלֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb days|יְמֵ֣י\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb is your portion|חֶלְקְךָ֙\rb* \rb in life|בַּֽחַיִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and in your labor|וּבַעֲמָ֣לְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָמֵ֖ל\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Whatever|כֹּ֠ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you find|תִּמְצָ֧א\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb with your hands|יָֽדְךָ֛\rb*, \rb do it|עֲשֵׂ֑ה\rb* \rb with all your might|בְּכֹחֲךָ֖\rb*, \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb in Sheol|בִּשְׁא֕וֹל\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are going|הֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb there is|שָֽׁמָּה׃ס\rb* \rb no|אֵ֨ין\rb* \rb work|מַעֲשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb or planning|וְחֶשְׁבּוֹן֙\rb* \rb or knowledge|וְדַ֣עַת\rb* \rb or wisdom|וְחָכְמָ֔ה\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb I saw|וְרָאֹ֣ה\rb* \rb something else|שַׁ֜בְתִּי\rb* \rb under|תַֽחַת־\rb* \rb the sun|הַשֶּׁ֗מֶשׁ\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb*: \rb The race|הַמֵּר֜וֹץ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֧א\rb* \rb is not|לֹא֩\rb* \rb to the swift|לַקַּלִּ֨ים\rb*, \rb nor the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb to the strong|לַגִּבּוֹרִ֣ים\rb*;\rb |וְ֠גַם\rb* \rb neither is|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb the bread|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb to the wise|לַחֲכָמִ֥ים\rb*, \rb nor|וְגַ֨ם\rb*\rb |לֹ֤א\rb* \rb the wealth|עֹ֔שֶׁר\rb* \rb to the intelligent|לַנְּבֹנִים֙\rb*, \rb nor|וְגַ֛ם\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb the favor|חֵ֑ן\rb* \rb to the skillful|לַיֹּדְעִ֖ים\rb*. \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb time|עֵ֥ת\rb* \rb and chance|וָפֶ֖גַע\rb* \rb happen|יִקְרֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to all|כֻּלָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb For|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb surely|גַּם֩\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb knows|יֵדַ֨ע\rb* \rb his time|עִתּ֗וֹ\rb*: \rb Like fish|כַּדָּגִים֙\rb* \rb caught|שֶׁנֶּֽאֱחָזִים֙\rb* \rb in a cruel|רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb net|בִּמְצוֹדָ֣ה\rb* \rb or birds|וְכַ֨צִּפֳּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb trapped|הָאֲחֻז֖וֹת\rb* \rb in a snare|בַּפָּ֑ח\rb*,\rb |כָּהֵ֗ם\rb* \rb so men|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb are ensnared|יֽוּקָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb in an evil|רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb time|לְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb that suddenly|פִּתְאֹֽם׃\rb* \rb falls|כְּשֶׁתִּפּ֥וֹל\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\s1 Wisdom Is Better than Strength
\p \v 13 \rb I have also seen|רָאִ֥יתִי\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֛ה\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and it|הִ֖יא\rb* \rb was great|וּגְדוֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*: \v 14 \rb There was a small|קְטַנָּ֔ה\rb* \rb city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb with few|מְעָ֑ט\rb* \rb men|וַאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb*. \rb A mighty|גָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb came|וּבָֽא־\rb* \rb against it|אֵלֶ֜יהָ\rb*, \rb surrounded it|וְסָבַ֣ב\rb*,\rb |אֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and built|וּבָנָ֥ה\rb* \rb large|גְּדֹלִֽים׃\rb* \rb siege ramps|מְצוֹדִ֥ים\rb* \rb against it|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Now a poor|מִסְכֵּן֙\rb* \rb wise|חָכָ֔ם\rb* \rb man|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb was found|וּמָ֣צָא\rb* \rb in the city|בָ֗הּ\rb*, \rb and he|ה֥וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saved|וּמִלַּט־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb by his wisdom|בְּחָכְמָת֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Yet no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb one|וְאָדָם֙\rb* \rb remembered|זָכַ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that|הַהּֽוּא׃\rb* \rb poor|הַמִּסְכֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֥ישׁ\rb*. \v 16 \rb And I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb said|וְאָמַ֣רְתִּי\rb*, “\rb Wisdom|חָכְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb is better|טוֹבָ֥ה\rb* \rb than strength|מִגְּבוּרָ֑ה\rb*, \rb but the wisdom|וְחָכְמַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the poor|הַמִּסְכֵּן֙\rb* \rb man is despised|בְּזוּיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and his words|וּדְבָרָ֖יו\rb* \rb are not|אֵינָ֥ם\rb* \rb heeded|נִשְׁמָעִֽים׃\rb*.”
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb The calm|בְּנַ֖חַת\rb* \rb words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the wise|חֲכָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb are heeded|נִשְׁמָעִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb over the shouts|מִזַּעֲקַ֥ת\rb* \rb of a ruler|מוֹשֵׁ֖ל\rb* \rb among fools|בַּכְּסִילִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb Wisdom|חָכְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb is better|טוֹבָ֥ה\rb* \rb than weapons|מִכְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of war|קְרָ֑ב\rb*,
\q2 \rb but one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb sinner|וְחוֹטֶ֣א\rb* \rb destroys|יְאַבֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb much|הַרְבֵּֽה׃\rb* \rb good|טוֹבָ֥ה\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 Wisdom and Folly
\q1 \v 1 \rb As dead|מָ֔וֶת\rb* \rb flies|זְב֣וּבֵי\rb* \rb bring|יַבִּ֖יעַ\rb* \rb a stench|יַבְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to the perfumer’s|רוֹקֵ֑חַ\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֣מֶן\rb*,
\q2 \rb so a little|מְעָֽט׃\rb* \rb folly|סִכְל֥וּת\rb* \rb outweighs|יָקָ֛ר\rb* \rb wisdom|מֵחָכְמָ֥ה\rb* \rb and honor|מִכָּב֖וֹד\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb A wise man’s|חָכָם֙\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֤ב\rb* \rb inclines to the right|לִֽימִינ֔וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the heart|וְלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb of a fool|כְּסִ֖יל\rb* \rb to the left|לִשְׂמֹאלֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb Even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb as the fool|כְּשֶׁהַסָּכָל\rb* \rb walks|הֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb along the road|בַּדֶּ֛רֶךְ\rb*, \rb his sense|לִבּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb is lacking|חָסֵ֑ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and he shows|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb everyone|לַכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb that he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is a fool|סָכָ֥ל\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb the ruler’s|הַמּוֹשֵׁל֙\rb* \rb temper|ר֤וּחַ\rb* \rb flares|תַּעֲלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb abandon|תַּנַּ֑ח\rb* \rb your post|מְקוֹמְךָ֖\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb calmness|מַרְפֵּ֔א\rb* \rb lays great|גְּדוֹלִֽים׃\rb* \rb offenses|חֲטָאִ֥ים\rb* \rb to rest|יַנִּ֖יחַ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb There is|יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb an evil|רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb I have seen|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb* —
\q2 \rb an error|כִּשְׁגָגָ֕ה\rb* \rb that proceeds|שֶׁיֹּצָ֖א\rb* \rb from|מִלִּפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the ruler|הַשַּׁלִּֽיט׃\rb*:
\q1 \v 6 \rb Folly|הַסֶּ֔כֶל\rb* \rb is appointed|נִתַּ֣ן\rb* \rb to great|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb heights|בַּמְּרוֹמִ֖ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the rich|וַעֲשִׁירִ֖ים\rb* \rb sit|יֵשֵֽׁבוּ׃\rb* \rb in lowly positions|בַּשֵּׁ֥פֶל\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb I have seen|רָאִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb slaves|עֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb horseback|סוּסִ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb while princes|וְשָׂרִ֛ים\rb* \rb go|הֹלְכִ֥ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb foot|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb like slaves|כַּעֲבָדִ֖ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb He who digs|חֹפֵ֥ר\rb* \rb a pit|גּוּמָּ֖ץ\rb* \rb may fall|יִפּ֑וֹל\rb* \rb into it|בּ֣וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and he who breaches|וּפֹרֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb a wall|גָּדֵ֖ר\rb* \rb may be bitten|יִשְּׁכֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb by a snake|נָחָֽשׁ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb The one who quarries|מַסִּ֣יעַ\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb may be injured|יֵעָצֵ֖ב\rb* \rb by them|בָּהֶ֑ם\rb*,
